# Keep the Docker build context lean and never leak data files or build output.
#
# Rationale: the multi-stage Dockerfile rebuilds the frontend and the backend
# from source inside the image, so build artifacts, dependency caches, and VCS
# metadata add nothing but bloat. Mounted data files (GeoLite2 .mmdb, CAIDA
# AS-relationship datasets) must NEVER enter an image; they are provided at
# runtime by volume mount.

# Rust build output
/target
**/target

# Node dependencies and build output (rebuilt inside the frontend stage)
**/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Version control and CI/agent metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules
.github

# Mounted, gitignored data files (defense in depth; also excluded by .gitignore)
/data
**/*.mmdb
**/*as-rel*
.env
.env.*

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Docs and local notes not needed to build
docs
*.md
!README.md
